From 564f9982a87625e006b8465bdb4a7deb51cf55e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hyunwoo Kim <imv4bel@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 06:42:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] inet: reject unhashed sockets during established lookups

Stable commit d69100340b4cae08d40f898f1b601032403f6be6
([ Upstream commit 4e2b3ef19e0e04adca38442f07dd6bc93c712bf1 ])
combines request-socket lifetime cleanup with the established-lookup guards
that consume those objects. The preceding downstream split contains the five
lifetime functions. This second split contains only the two lookup guards and
must follow the lifetime stage.

TCP established ehash lookups are lockless. The socket caches involved use
SLAB_TYPESAFE_BY_RCU, so memory can be reused before an RCU reader that
retained its old address has finished.

After a tuple match, __inet_lookup_established() and
__inet6_lookup_established() acquire a reference and repeat the tuple check.
They did not check whether the new object was hashed. If the address was
reused for a socket with the same tuple, the lookup could acquire a reference
to the new object and return it while its nulls node was unhashed.

After taking a reference, check whether the nulls node is unhashed in both
IPv4 and IPv6 established lookups. If it is unhashed or the tuple no longer
matches, drop the reference and restart the lookup. Lookups racing with the
TIME_WAIT hashdance, or with a request being replaced by its child, then
restart and find the new socket instead of returning the old one.

This stage changes only __inet_lookup_established() and
__inet6_lookup_established(). Together with the preceding lifetime split it
reconstructs the stable change and first completes the CVE-2026-99288
correction.

The split retains the stable commit's code exactly in these two functions.
The final two-stage tree-equivalence proof is recorded with the livepatch
release evidence.

Fixes: 079096f103fa ("tcp/dccp: install syn_recv requests into ehash table")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Hyunwoo Kim <imv4bel@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Eric Dumazet <edumazet@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Kuniyuki Iwashima <kuniyu@google.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261029214219.1035176-2-imv4bel@gmail.com
Signed-off-by: Paolo Abeni <pabeni@redhat.com>
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 net/ipv4/inet_hashtables.c  | 5 +++--
 net/ipv6/inet6_hashtables.c | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/ipv4/inet_hashtables.c b/net/ipv4/inet_hashtables.c
index 37a6acff537e6..e8adf8530596c 100644
--- a/net/ipv4/inet_hashtables.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/inet_hashtables.c
@@ -512,8 +512,9 @@ struct sock *__inet_lookup_established(const struct net *net,
 		if (likely(inet_match(net, sk, acookie, ports, dif, sdif))) {
 			if (unlikely(!refcount_inc_not_zero(&sk->sk_refcnt)))
 				goto out;
-			if (unlikely(!inet_match(net, sk, acookie,
-						 ports, dif, sdif))) {
+			if (unlikely(hlist_nulls_unhashed_lockless(&sk->sk_nulls_node) ||
+				     !inet_match(net, sk, acookie, ports, dif,
+						 sdif))) {
 				sock_gen_put(sk);
 				goto begin;
 			}
diff --git a/net/ipv6/inet6_hashtables.c b/net/ipv6/inet6_hashtables.c
index 9ec05e354baa6..70633fed6e6af 100644
--- a/net/ipv6/inet6_hashtables.c
+++ b/net/ipv6/inet6_hashtables.c
@@ -74,7 +74,9 @@ struct sock *__inet6_lookup_established(const struct net *net,
 		if (unlikely(!refcount_inc_not_zero(&sk->sk_refcnt)))
 			goto out;
 
-		if (unlikely(!inet6_match(net, sk, saddr, daddr, ports, dif, sdif))) {
+		if (unlikely(hlist_nulls_unhashed_lockless(&sk->sk_nulls_node) ||
+			     !inet6_match(net, sk, saddr, daddr, ports, dif,
+					  sdif))) {
 			sock_gen_put(sk);
 			goto begin;
 		}
